' #FISSURE-PLUGIN 1
' #NAME "Generic Command Probe Adapter"
' #TYPE TEST
' #REQUIRES GRAPH.WRITE
'
' RFC section 17 lists this as the reference TEST extension (alongside a more specific ctest.ab,
' which auto-discovers tests from an existing CTest suite -- real, named future work, not built
' this session; see AGENT_PROGRESS.md). command.ab is the generic case: any project can register a
' probe as "run this shell command," with an explicit, human-declared dependency list, without
' Fissure needing to understand what produced that command at all (RFC section 9's own example:
' `probe: id / runner / tags`, no test-framework-specific fields).
'
' A project's own fissure.ab config calls this instead of the raw FISSURE.Probe.* contracts
' directly -- e.g.:
'
'     ignored = RegisterCommandProbe("compiler.parser.basic", "ctest --test-dir build -R parser_basic", ["parser"], ["src/compiler/parser.cpp"])
'
' `dependsOn` is the probe's declared file dependency set (RFC section 5.3 "Declared" evidence,
' AGENT_PROGRESS.md's Session 1 design decision 1 -- exactly what lets a probe ever be classified
' UNAFFECTED rather than UNKNOWN). Pass an empty array for a probe with no known dependencies yet;
' it will simply run every time (UNKNOWN, per the safety invariant) until someone declares one.

FUNCTION RegisterCommandProbe(id, command, tags, dependsOn)
    ignored = FISSURE.Probe.Register(id, command, tags)
    FOR path IN dependsOn
        ignored = FISSURE.Probe.DependsOn(id, path)
    NEXT
END FUNCTION
